{
  "title": "AWS Solutions Architect Anki Deck + AnkiConnect Automation System",
  "content": "## Plan Overview\n\nThis plan creates a complete Anki-based study system for AWS Solutions Architect Associate (SAA-C03) certification with three major deliverables:\n\n1. **Anki Deck (.apkg)** - Structured deck with ~150 cards across 5 core AWS domains mapped to the official exam syllabus\n2. **Python Automation Scripts** - AnkiConnect-based scripts for adding/updating cards, detecting weak items (retention <75% or ease <1.8), and managing the deck programmatically\n3. **Documentation** - Setup guide, usage instructions, and scheduling rules\n\n### Approach\n- Research the exact SAA-C03 exam guide for domain weights and topic mapping\n- Build deck structure and card content in parallel with automation scripts\n- Create scheduling/priority logic that weights by both weakness metrics AND syllabus domain importance\n- Synthesize all deliverables with comprehensive documentation\n\n### Domain Weight Mapping (SAA-C03):\n- Domain 1: Design Secure Architectures (30%)\n- Domain 2: Design Resilient Architectures (26%)\n- Domain 3: Design High-Performing Architectures (24%)\n- Domain 4: Design Cost-Optimized Architectures (20%)\n\nCards span EC2, S3, RDS, IAM, and Networking mapped into these domains.",
  "tasks": [
    {
      "goal": "Fetch the official AWS SAA-C03 exam guide PDF to extract exact domain breakdowns, topic weights, and sub-topic details for accurate syllabus mapping",
      "tool_name": "web_fetch",
      "depends_on": []
    },
    {
      "goal": "Research AnkiConnect API documentation - fetch the full API reference to understand available endpoints for deck creation, card management, note operations, and scheduling manipulation",
      "tool_name": "web_fetch",
      "depends_on": []
    },
    {
      "goal": "Build the complete Anki deck package: Create a Python script that generates an .apkg file with hierarchical deck structure (AWS_SAA::Domain1_Secure_Architectures, AWS_SAA::Domain2_Resilient, etc.), custom note types with fields for Question/Answer/Explanation/Domain/SubTopic/DifficultyLevel/ExamWeight, and ~150 high-quality cards across EC2 (30 cards), S3 (30 cards), RDS (30 cards), IAM (30 cards), and VPC/Networking (30 cards). Cards should include conceptual recall, scenario-based, and comparison-type questions. Use the genanki library. Include domain weight metadata in tags. Output the .apkg file and the generation script.",
      "tool_name": "spawn_sub_agent",
      "depends_on": [0]
    },
    {
      "goal": "Build the AnkiConnect automation scripts suite: (1) anki_card_manager.py - CRUD operations for cards via AnkiConnect API (add single/bulk cards, update existing cards, delete cards, search by tag/deck/domain), (2) anki_weak_item_detector.py - queries Anki stats to find cards with retention <75% or ease factor <1.8, outputs a weakness report grouped by domain with severity scores, (3) anki_gap_filler.py - takes weakness report and auto-generates new cards for weak topics or reschedules existing weak cards with boosted priority, (4) anki_sync.py - master orchestration script that runs detection → gap filling → scheduling in one command. All scripts should use Python requests library targeting AnkiConnect localhost:8765. Include proper error handling, logging, and configuration via a config.yaml file for thresholds and preferences.",
      "tool_name": "spawn_sub_agent",
      "depends_on": [1]
    },
    {
      "goal": "Build the scheduling and priority engine: Create anki_scheduler.py that implements (1) custom priority scoring combining Anki ease factor + retention rate + domain exam weight (Domain 1=30%, Domain 2=26%, Domain 3=24%, Domain 4=20%) + days-until-exam factor for 8-week timeline, (2) a daily study plan generator that recommends which cards to focus on based on the priority score, allocating more time to high-weight weak domains, (3) weekly progress dashboard that shows retention by domain and flags domains below target, (4) SM-2 compatible interval modifications that shorten intervals for weak+high-weight items and lengthen for strong+low-weight items. Output as a standalone Python module with CLI interface.",
      "tool_name": "spawn_claude_code_agent",
      "depends_on": [1]
    },
    {
      "goal": "Synthesize all deliverables and create comprehensive documentation: (1) README.md with project overview, prerequisites (Anki, AnkiConnect addon installation instructions, Python 3.8+), quick start guide, (2) SETUP.md with step-by-step installation and configuration, (3) USAGE.md with detailed usage examples for each script including CLI flags and config.yaml options, (4) ARCHITECTURE.md explaining deck structure rationale, domain-to-subdeck mapping, card type design decisions, scheduling algorithm explanation, (5) Verify all scripts are consistent in their interfaces and config format, (6) Create a requirements.txt with all dependencies, (7) Create a Makefile or run.sh for common workflows (detect-weak, generate-report, fill-gaps, full-sync). Package everything into a coherent project structure.",
      "tool_name": "spawn_sub_agent",
      "depends_on": [2, 3, 4]
    }
  ],
